The fact-check confirms that rock musician Jon Bon Jovi performed acoustically at a drive-in campaign event for Joe Biden, who was the Democratic presidential nominee, in Luzerne County, Pennsylvania, on [October 24, 2020](https://www.app.com/story/entertainment/music/2020/10/24/jon-bon-jovi-hitting-campaign-trail-big-i-vote-concert-support-biden/6022327002/). However, the available evidence [does not specify the number of attendees](https://www.gettyimages.com/editorial-images/news/event/joe-biden-campaigns-for-president-in-pennsylvania/775580699) and [makes no mention of pumpkins](https://spectrumlocalnews.com/ap-top-news/2020/10/24/the-latest-trump-voting-in-florida-bon-jovi-joining-biden) being present at the event. Due to the lack of verification for the specific numerical claims of "12 people and 7 pumpkins," the final verdict is **not enough information**.